// Behavioral fixture — the demo go_fish scratch-pile ask pattern
// (deterministic: no shuffle) — via the memory-backed ask: the choose stores
// the rank in `AskRank` (+ `AskFlag` marker) and the shared transfer/draw
// block below reads it back, exactly as test_games/go_fish.cgdsl does now.
// Same deck/hands as behavior_go_fish_ask: after dealing 7:
//   P1 = [Ace-D, Ace-C, Ace-H, Two-D, Two-C, Two-H, Three-D],
//   P2 = [Three-C, Three-H, Four-D, Four-C, Four-H, Five-D, Five-C],
//   Deck = [Eight-D, Eight-C, Eight-H].
// P1 asks a *chosen* player (`of any`, scripted to P2) via the Scratch pile:
//   - ask "Three" (P2 holds it)  -> transfer both, NO draw (regression: the
//     draw check must run BEFORE the take — the take empties Scratch, so a
//     later `Scratch empty` check would draw on hits too);
//   - ask "Ace" (P2 lacks it)    -> draw exactly 1.
player P1, P2, P3
turnorder (P:P1, P:P2, P:P3)
location Hand on all
location Deck on table
location Scratch on table
memory AskRank on all
memory AskFlag on all

card on Deck:
  Rank(Ace, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven, Eight)
    for Suit(Diamonds, Clubs, Hearts)

stage Deal for current 1 times {
  deal 7 from Deck private to Hand of all
}

stage Ask for current 1 times {
  reset AskRank
  reset AskFlag
  choose {
    if ("Three" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Three"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("Ace" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Ace"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
  }
  if ((&I:AskFlag of current) == 1) {
    deal Hand where Rank is (&S:AskRank of current) of any private to Scratch
    if (Scratch empty) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    if (not Scratch empty) {
      deal Scratch private to Hand of current
    }
  }
  end stage
}
